# Tooling for registering a model, kept out of requirements.in on purpose.
#
# MLflow and its dependencies add well over a hundred megabytes to an image that only needs
# to read a CSV, score it and write a CSV back. Lab 5 measured the container registry at
# 38% of that project's bill, nearly all of it images nobody deletes, so an unused
# dependency in the serving image is a recurring cost rather than an untidiness.
#
# Install with:
#     uv pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-registry.txt
-r requirements.in
mlflow==3.16.1
